index db7a4140..bcc4d6dc 100644
--- a/docs/source-en/rst_source/concepts/channel.rst
+++ b/docs/source-en/rst_source/concepts/channel.rst
@@ -40,6 +40,30 @@ A distributed channel binds each ``key`` to one replica the first time that key
 Code already running inside a worker may instead call
 ``self.create_channel(...)`` or ``self.connect_channel("Samples")``.
 
+Select Ray CPU Object Transport
+-------------------------------
+
+Worker handles use collective send/recv by default. To exchange CPU tensors and
+serializable objects through Ray without initializing a collective group, select
+the transport explicitly:
+
+.. code-block:: python
+
+   sample_channel = Channel.create(name="SamplesCPU", transport="ray")
+   producer_group.produce(sample_channel)
+   consumer_group.consume(sample_channel)
+
+The setting travels with a serialized handle. A new connection by name must
+select it again with ``self.connect_channel("SamplesCPU", transport="ray")`` or
+``Channel.connect(name, current_worker, transport="ray")``. The existing queue
+can serve either type of handle; the transport belongs to the handle. Collectors,
+dispatcher consumer routing, keys, weights, and async operations still apply.
+
+Ray object transport is intended for CPU payloads. Copy accelerator tensors to
+CPU before putting them into the channel. It does not validate GPU collective
+communication or provide the same throughput, and cannot be combined with
+``local=True``.
+
 Put, Get, and Batch Items
 -------------------------
 
